{"id":"NCT06366464","title":"A Study of Pitolisant in Patients With Prader-Willi Syndrome","official":"A Phase 3, Randomized, Double-Blind, Placebo-controlled, Efficacy and Safety Study of Pitolisant Followed by an Open-Label Extension in Patients With Prader-Willi Syndrome","summary":"This is a Phase 3, randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled, multicenter, global clinical study to assess the efficacy and safety of pitolisant in patients living with Prader-Willi syndrome.\n\nThe primary objective of this study is to evaluate the efficacy of pitolisant in treating excessive daytime sleepiness (EDS) in patients ≥6 years of age with Prader-Willi syndrome.\n\nSecondary objectives include assessing the impact of pitolisant on:\n\nIrritable and disruptive behaviors Hyperphagia Other behavioral problems including social withdrawal, stereotypic behavior, hyperactivity/noncompliance, and inappropriate speech","conditions":["Prader-Willi Syndrome"],"interventions":[{"type":"DRUG","name":"Pitolisant tablet"},{"type":"OTHER","name":"Placebo tablet"}],"criteria":"Inclusion Criteria:\n\n* Genetically confirmed diagnosis of PWS\n* Excessive daytime sleepiness\n* Has a consistent parent/caregiver (preferably the same person throughout the study) who is willing and able to complete the required study assessments.\n* In the opinion of the Investigator, the patient/parent(s)/caregiver(s)/legal guardian(s) are capable of understanding and complying with the requirements of the protocol and administration of oral study drug.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n\n* Has a diagnosis of sleep apnea (OSA, CSA) that is not adequately controlled\n* Has a diagnosis of hypersomnia due to another sleep/medical disorder\n* Participation in an interventional research study involving another investigational medication, device, or behavioral treatment within 30 days or 5 half-lives (whichever is longer) of the investigational medication prior to Screening","minAge":"6 Years","maxAge":"","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"INTERVENTIONAL","purpose":"TREATMENT","enrollment":134,"start":"2024-05-28","pcd":"2027-04","upd":"2026-08-25","sponsor":"Harmony Biosciences Management, Inc.","areas":["other","rare"],"central":["Ann Adee · 773-383-6258 · clinicaltrials@harmonybiosciences.com","Linnea Ryan · clinicaltrials@harmonybiosciences.com"],"sites":[{"f":"Santa Monica Clinical Trials","city":"Los Angeles","pr":"California","zip":"90025","s":"R","lat":34.0522,"lon":-118.2437,"c":"Samantha Montenez · 310-586-0843 · e. smontanez@smclinicaltrials.com"},{"f":"Center of Excellence in Diabetes and Endocrinology","city":"Sacramento","pr":"California","zip":"95821-2123","s":"R","lat":38.5816,"lon":-121.4944,"c":"Natalie Marlen · 279-210-9814 · marlenn@sutterhealth.org"},{"f":"Rady Children's Hospital - Scan Diego","city":"San Diego","pr":"California","zip":"92123","s":"R","lat":32.7157,"lon":-117.1647,"c":"Megan Warner · mwarner2@rchsd.org"},{"f":"Colorado Children's Hospital","city":"Aurora","pr":"Colorado","zip":"80045","s":"R","lat":39.7294,"lon":-104.8319,"c":"Nathan Holly · 920-264-4742 · nathan.holly@childrenscolorado.org"},{"f":"Nemours Children's Hospital","city":"Wilmington","pr":"Delaware","zip":"19803-3607","s":"R","lat":39.746,"lon":-75.5466,"c":"Kimberly Renner · 302-651-6400 · kimberly.renner@nemours.org"},{"f":"Atlanta Diabetes Associates","city":"Atlanta","pr":"Georgia","zip":"30318","s":"STOP","lat":33.749,"lon":-84.388,"c":""},{"f":"Emory University School of Medicine","city":"Atlanta","pr":"Georgia","zip":"30322","s":"R","lat":33.749,"lon":-84.388,"c":"Gwendolyn Gunn · 404-778-8552 · gwendolyn.gisiner.gunn@emory.edu"},{"f":"Rare Disease Research","city":"Atlanta","pr":"Georgia","zip":"30329","s":"STOP","lat":33.749,"lon":-84.388,"c":""},{"f":"Ann And Robert H Lurie Children's Hospital of Chicago","city":"Chicago","pr":"Illinois","zip":"60611","s":"R","lat":41.85,"lon":-87.65,"c":"Sarayu Ratnam, PhD · 312-227-6617 · sratnam@luriechildrens.org"},{"f":"Riley Child